The '''Kadas'sa'Nikto''', or '''Green Nikto''', were one of the [[subspecies]] of the [[Nikto]] [[species]] from the [[planet]] [[Kintan]]; another was the [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]]. They had scaly [[Color|green]], gray, or red skin, black eyes, and symmetrical horns.

==Biology and appearance==
The Kadas'sa'Nikto, also known as the Green Nikto,<ref name="Calendar">[[Star Wars Day-at-a-Time Calendar 2021|''Star Wars'' Day-at-a-Time Calendar 2021]]</ref> were a [[subspecies]] of the [[Sentience|sentient]] [[humanoid]] [[Nikto]] [[species]] from the [[planet]] [[Kintan]]. Like their cousins the [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]], they had scaly [[Color|green]] or gray skin, black eyes, and symmetrical horns.<ref name="DB" /> Kadas'sa'Nikto were able to sustain and survive in harsh [[desert]] climates.<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> Members of the species could be [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="TCVD NE">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> Falling rain was refreshing for the scales of a Kadas'sa'Nikto.<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref>

==Kadas'sa'Nikto in the galaxy==
Several Kadas'sa'Nikto became members of the [[Jedi Order]] and served as guardians of the [[Galactic Republic]]. [[Aida Forte]] was a [[Jedi Knight]] in the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Convergence">''[[The High Republic: Convergence]]''</ref> Forte's friend and fellow [[Jedi]], [[Creighton Sun]], thought the eyes of the Kadas'sa'Nikto species were beautiful, with Sun also making note of a bright optimism that always seemed to fill Forte's eyes. During the [[Night of Sorrow|Battle of Dalna]], he watched as her eyes filled with rain and tears shortly before her death.<ref name="Cataclysm" /> During the later stages of the [[Clone Wars]], [[Jedi Master]] [[J'oopi Shé]] was part of the Order's [[Technical division]] and was stationed in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the planet [[Coruscant]].<ref name="TCVD NE" /> [[Nuhj]] was a Kadas'sa'Nikto [[Jedi]] who initially survived [[Order 66]] by hiding on [[Anoat]] and later [[Burnin Konn]], but he was ultimately [[Death|killed]] by an [[Inquisitor]].<ref name="Uprising">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''</ref>

Due to their biological characteristics, Kadas'sa'Nikto were ideal enforcers for the [[Hutt Clan]].<ref name="Battlefront II" /> The [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]] employed Kadas'sa'Nikto individuals in his [[Jabba's criminal empire|criminal empire]] on [[Tatooine]]. These included [[Wooof]], who was in charge of Jabba's fleet of [[skiff]]s and the [[sail barge]] ''[[Khetanna]]'';<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> [[Klaatu]], who helped repair the skiffs<ref name="USW NE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> and served as a [[bodyguard]];<ref name="Beware the Power of the Dark Side">''[[Return of the Jedi: Beware the Power of the Dark Side!]]''</ref> and [[Giran]], who worked in [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]].<ref name="SWCE">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

As the [[Galactic Empire]]'s control in their [[sector]] became unbearable, some green Niktos joined the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], whether to seek liberty and justice for [[the galaxy]] or due to more selfish motivations. After the fall of the Empire, many green Niktos fought for control of what was left behind, although some remained loyal to [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] as she sent out a call to arms against the [[First Order]].<ref name="Battlefront II" />

During the [[New Republic era]], one Kadas'sa'Nikto named [[Neeku Vozo]] worked as a [[Technician|mechanic]] at the former [[New Republic]] [[starfighter]] [[pilot]] [[Jarek Yeager]]'s [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station|repair shop]] on the ''[[Colossus]]'', a [[supertanker fuel depot]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[ocean]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Castilon]].<ref name="The Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref>

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Kadas'sa'Nikto first appeared in the [[1983]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> In the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] continuity, they were first identified in the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''.<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

